    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and produces trustworthy performance numbers. It is written to be executed by an engineer who did not build the system, because the most common failure mode in distributed validation is the builder unconsciously confirming their own assumptions.\n\n**Ground rule:** every item below must produce an artifact (log line, file, screenshot, or recorded command output). A check that leaves no evidence was not performed.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pre-Conditions and Environment Pinning\n\nBefore touching the serving system itself, freeze the environment so results are attributable.\n\n- [ ] **Record the exact artifact under test.** Model checkpoint hash, tokenizer hash, serving binary/container digest, scheduler version, and any post-training adapter weights. \"The build from Tuesday\" is not an identity.\n- [ ] **Record hardware topology per node:** GPU count/model per node, NVLink/NVSwitch topology, interconnect (IB/RoCE/Ethernet) with link speeds, and NIC-to-GPU affinity. Note any heterogeneity across nodes \u2014 asymmetric nodes invalidate many later assumptions.\n- [ ] **Record software stack versions:** driver, CUDA/ROCm, NCCL/HCCL/Gloo, MPI if present, Python, and the inference engine version. Capture `nccl-tests` or equivalent all-reduce bandwidth results as a baseline sanity number.\n- [ ] **Confirm clock synchronization** across nodes (chrony/PTP status, max observed skew). If skew exceeds your timing tolerance (see \u00a75), flag it now, not after the benchmark.\n- [ ] **Verify clean state:** no leftover processes from prior runs, no stale shared-memory segments, no residual GPU memory from crashed ranks. A \"warm\" system from a previous experiment is a",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
